# Exact V4 effect commitment recipe — proposed author agreement

The pure helper owner must be EraseIntentStore. It returns existing EraseSchema2ColdControlEffectV1 DATA only; private Router must actually issue a revocable one-effect permit proving the exact scope/source/physical cut and genuine receipt identities. This is an additional concrete source/interface proposal for independent review, not an implemented helper or minted permit. Existing V1 kind strings remain unchanged; V4 must not call the old helper whose4096-byte path predicate would reject lawful inputs.

Binary input to SHA256: ASCIIARS2EF04(8), opcodeU8, eraseUUID16, operationUUID16, phaseU8(P1/Q2/R3/C4 mapping actual EraseIntentPhase), optional expectedCanonicalSHA(tag+32), optional assignedPath(tag+lengthU64+exactUTF8), inputCountU16, exact ordered SHA32 commitments below. ExpectedCanonicalSHA is the actual incumbent targeted fixed control SHA when applicable; it is nil only for genuine creation/read/noncanonical effect. AssignedPath is nil for aggregate read/publication or the exact authenticated target path for one-source/control effect. No caller-selectedkind/path/count/table membership is authority. Stage/ordinal currentness and every source/receipt are proved through actual private origin before/after each effect; unknown opcode/input count/tag refuses. Scalar hashes encode exact existing text or explicit fixed numeric framing (never JSON escaped strings); source/target ordinals have fixed UInt64 width and exact checked conversions. A listed absent tag is SHA256(single closed tagU8) from actual explicit original/data state, not a default hash for a missing getter.

