Sources/record cuts are the actual authenticated private observed cuts, separately issued before these APIs; publication input recipes are semantic commitments only after actual source-backed count/chain passes. No API guesses a future currentcut or uses this helper to issue a Source/EX/G/progress capability. Any multi-field scalar hash in the table uses each numeric field fixed-width and each text lengthU64 before UTF8; this is injective even for arbitrary admitted strings. RequestCommitment additionally binds planSHA, stepSHA, producer ordinal/role/path, exact temp, mode, payloadSHA/count and actual input recordBinding in that order. LastLeaf/RootRemoval dataCommitment describes their actual already-completed receipt DATA, but real authority methods still require the exact private receipt OBJECT; SHA equality alone never suffices. Actual OS readback remains the real privately consumed object, never a digest input that can stand in for removal/readback.

Nested private Store reads preserve the outer operation's effect rather than requesting an unrelated read permit. Own checked publication attempt authenticates exact already-observed physical child readback derivations within one predeclared source/Progress/terminal program; it cannot append a semantic source or birth. Any failed check/effect/readback poisons the actual owner/permit and retains uncertainty. Scope revocation precedes genuine G/EX release. Actual makeV4ControlEffect implementation and all counterpart caller construction remain source prerequisites; source oldbytes/formats are unchanged.
